● Decision Tree Classifier

  A Decision Tree splits data into branches based on feature conditions, like a flowchart of if-else rules. It keeps
  splitting until it reaches a pure leaf node with a class label. It is easy to interpret and visualize. Works well for
  both classification and regression tasks.

  ---
  Naive Bayes

  Naive Bayes is a probabilistic classifier based on Bayes' Theorem that assumes all features are independent. It
  calculates the probability of each class given the input features and picks the highest. It is fast, simple, and works
  exceptionally well for text classification. Despite the "naive" independence assumption, it performs surprisingly well
  in real-world problems.

