> difference between supervised and unsupervised

● Supervised vs Unsupervised Learning

  ---
  Supervised Learning

  - Trains on labeled data (input + correct output)
  - Learns to predict output for new inputs
  - Like a student learning with an answer key

  Input: Email text → Label: Spam / Not Spam
  Input: House size → Label: Price

  ---
  Unsupervised Learning

  - Trains on unlabeled data (input only, no output)
  - Learns to find hidden patterns on its own
  - Like a student learning without an answer key

  Input: Customer data → Finds groups automatically
  Input: Images → Groups similar images together

  ---
  Key Differences

  ┌──────────────┬───────────────────────────────────────────────┬───────────────────┐
  │   Feature    │                  Supervised                   │   Unsupervised    │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Data         │ Labeled                                       │ Unlabeled         │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Output       │ Predefined                                    │ Unknown           │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Goal         │ Predict                                       │ Discover patterns │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Human effort │ High (labeling)                               │ Low               │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Accuracy     │ Measurable                                    │ Hard to measure   │
  ├──────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────┼───────────────────┤
  │ Examples     │ Decision Tree, Naive Bayes, Linear Regression │ K-Means, DBSCAN   │
  └──────────────┴───────────────────────────────────────────────┴───────────────────┘

  ---
  Real-Life Analogy

